 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "pXqogyxGAQAJ",
   "from": "Matthew Smith",
   "author": "e1b65c2d8ed36d3a",
   "date": "2024-06-27T12:42:54Z",
   "subject": "Visualise ROI masks in v3.6",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hello,<div><br></div><div>I am struggling to visualise my selected ROIs as masks over my image with v3.6.</div><div><br></div><div>With the previous version I used:</div><div><font color=\"#ff0000\">levels = makeFactor(L1 = ..., L2 = ..., ...)</font></div><div><font color=\"#ff0000\">image(MSIobject, levels ~ x * y, key=T)</font><br></div><div><br></div><div>However, I now get the error:</div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><font color=\"#ff0000\">Error in <a href=\"http://rep.int\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://rep.int&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793240466179000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Ns_pHFdvpFkCaY6EArTBU\">rep.int</a>(list(X), nrow(vals)) : \r\n  invalid type (NULL) for &#39;times&#39; (must be a vector)</font></span></span><br></div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\">\r\n<span style=\"color:rgba(0,0,0,0.87);font-family:Roboto,RobotoDraft,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">If I attach it to the spectra data I can generate the masks, but I lose the factor names</span></span></span></div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><font color=\"#ff0000\">spectra(cal_mix, &quot;levels&quot;) = t(levels)</font><span style=\"color:rgba(0,0,0,0.87);font-family:Roboto,RobotoDraft,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></span></span></span></div><div><br></div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"color:rgba(0,0,0,0.87);font-family:Roboto,RobotoDraft,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Is there a better way to do this?</span></span></span></div><div><br></div><div>Best wishes,</div><div>Matt</div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\">\r\n\r\n</span></span></div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\">\r\n\r\n</span></span></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "rjwAig5YAQAJ",
   "from": "kbemis",
   "author": "6033d3c0e7d242fa",
   "date": "2024-06-27T18:10:37Z",
   "subject": "Re: Visualise ROI masks in v3.6",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Add the variable as a column to the <font face=\"Courier New\">pixelData</font>.<div><br></div><div><font face=\"Courier New\">pData(MSIobject)$levels &lt;- levels</font></div><div><font face=\"Courier New\">image(MSIobject, &quot;levels&quot;) # simplest way</font></div><div><font face=\"Courier New\">image(MSIobject, levels ~ x * y, i=NULL) # alternative way<br></font></div><div><br></div><div>These should work. Passing just a character vector as the 2nd argument will look for the column(s) in <font face=\"Courier New\">pixelData</font>. If using a formula, setting <font face=\"Courier New\">i=NULL</font> says to look in <font face=\"Courier New\">pixelData</font> rather than <font face=\"Courier New\">spectraData</font> (where <font face=\"Courier New\">i</font> is used to resolve the rows of the intensity matrix).</div><div><br></div><div>The code for correctly resolving names in the formula that aren&#39;t part of the object were very subject to breaking, so 3.6 now has stricter rules for resolving these names as above.</div><div><br></div><div>You can find an example here:</div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/vignettes/Cardinal/inst/doc/Cardinal3-guide.html#summarization-e.g.-mean-spectra-tic-etc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/vignettes/Cardinal/inst/doc/Cardinal3-guide.html%23summarization-e.g.-mean-spectra-tic-etc&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793240466181000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0KVD1v1ll11dHlgLdLqB_x\">https://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/vignettes/Cardinal/inst/doc/Cardinal3-guide.html#summarization-e.g.-mean-spectra-tic-etc</a>.<br><br></div><div>-Kylie</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Thursday, June 27, 2024 at 8:42:54 AM UTC-4 <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mattyjs...@gmail.com</a> wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">Hello,<div><br></div><div>I am struggling to visualise my selected ROIs as masks over my image with v3.6.</div><div><br></div><div>With the previous version I used:</div><div><font color=\"#ff0000\">levels = makeFactor(L1 = ..., L2 = ..., ...)</font></div><div><font color=\"#ff0000\">image(MSIobject, levels ~ x * y, key=T)</font><br></div><div><br></div><div>However, I now get the error:</div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><font color=\"#ff0000\">Error in <a href=\"http://rep.int\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://rep.int&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793240466181000&amp;usg=AOvVaw02lZrr7UWvNs32wKwjf941\">rep.int</a>(list(X), nrow(vals)) : \r\n  invalid type (NULL) for &#39;times&#39; (must be a vector)</font></span></span><br></div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\">\r\n<span style=\"color:rgba(0,0,0,0.87);font-family:Roboto,RobotoDraft,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">If I attach it to the spectra data I can generate the masks, but I lose the factor names</span></span></span></div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><font color=\"#ff0000\">spectra(cal_mix, &quot;levels&quot;) = t(levels)</font><span style=\"color:rgba(0,0,0,0.87);font-family:Roboto,RobotoDraft,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></span></span></span></div><div><br></div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"color:rgba(0,0,0,0.87);font-family:Roboto,RobotoDraft,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Is there a better way to do this?</span></span></span></div><div><br></div><div>Best wishes,</div><div>Matt</div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\">\r\n\r\n</span></span></div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\">\r\n\r\n</span></span></div></blockquote></div>"
    ]
